            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospitalisation of your patient, a 58-year-old male, admitted on 05/01/2008 with an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, he presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed the exacerbation. Spirometry supported the diagnosis of significant airflow obstruction. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. Blood tests were performed to exclude infection and monitor inflammatory markers. He responded well to treatment with improvement in respiratory function and oxygen saturation. He was discharged on 06/01/2008 with oral steroids, inhaled bronchodilators, and written instructions. Please arrange early follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Yours sincerely, Dr. [Hospital Physician]</div>
               </text>
            </section>
